            "section": "Section C",
            "type": "subjective",
            "marks": 3,
            "question": "If $x+y+z=0$, prove that $x^3+y^3+z^3=3xyz$.",
            "finalAnswer": "Proof",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "Use identity: $x^3+y^3+z^3-3xyz = (x+y+z)(x^2+y^2+z^2-xy-yz-zx)$.",
                "Substitute $x+y+z=0$, then $x^3+y^3+z^3-3xyz = 0 \\\\implies x^3+y^3+z^3 = 3xyz$."
            ]
        },
