            "question": "Diagonal AC of a parallelogram ABCD bisects $\\angle A$. Show that: \\ni) it bisects $\\angle C$ also, \\nii) ABCD is a rhombus.",
            "finalAnswer": "Proof",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "i) Parallel lines: $\\\\angle DAC = \\\\angle BCA$. $\\\\angle BAC = \\\\angle DCA$. Since $\\\\angle DAC = \\\\angle BAC$, then $\\\\angle BCA = \\\\angle DCA$. So it bisects $\\\\angle C$.",
                "ii) In $\\\\triangle ABC$, $\\\\angle BAC = \\\\angle BCA \\\\implies AB = BC$. Adjacent sides are equal, so it's a rhombus."
            ]
