            "question": "Case Study 1: Polynomials \\nFactorise $x^3 - 23x^2 + 142x - 120$. \\ni) Find one factor using trial method. (2 Marks) \\nii) Factorise fully. (3 Marks)",
            "finalAnswer": "i) (x-1), ii) (x-1)(x-10)(x-12)",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "i) $P(1) = 1 - 23 + 142 - 120 = 0$. So (x-1) is a factor.",
                "ii) $(x-1)(x^2 - 22x + 120) = (x-1)(x-10)(x-12)$."
            ]
